# id <= 0 (including the default-initialized 0) means "no filter": return every
# currently tracked object. A specific positive id returns just that one tracked
# object, or an empty `objects` array if no tracked object currently has that id.
#
# Deliberately a single optional numeric filter field + an array response, so a
# future label filter (explicitly deferred - not implemented here) can be added
# as one more optional request field without changing the response shape.
int32 id
---
TrackedObject[] objects
